<!--
  CNC.Contracts - the wire contract between the machine server and any client (step 6 of the
  client/server split).

  THE RULE THAT KEEPS THIS ASSEMBLY HONEST: if it couldn't be JSON, it doesn't belong here.
  Plain data types only - no behavior, no events, no INotifyPropertyChanged, no references to any
  other project. A browser client consumes the JSON form of exactly these shapes; anything in here
  a browser couldn't also have is the pass-C#-objects shortcut sneaking back in.

  Namespaces: types MOVED here from CNC Core keep their original namespace (CNC.Core / CNC.GCode) so
  the move needed zero call-site churn - same zero-churn discipline as the step-5 forwarders. NEW
  contract types (the wire messages) use CNC.Contracts.

  This is the LEGACY net462 project the solution builds. CNC.Contracts.net8.csproj (same folder,
  same sources, NOT in the .sln) is the portability probe, built with dotnet - the same two-project
  pattern as CNC Core / CNC.Core.net8, and for the same reason: the VS MSBuild on this box (17.6)
  cannot resolve an SDK-style project targeting net8.0, so SDK-style projects stay out of the .sln.
-->
